      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "CRC errors on the physical interface of 172.16.4.22 are a very strong indicator of a physical layer problem, which is much more likely than just traffic congestion. These errors mean data packets are being corrupted as they travel across the wire, which causes the erratic jitter you are seeing. It's very common for these errors to be caused by a failing SFP module or electromagnetic interference (EMI) near the cabling. You should definitely investigate the SFP and the cable run immediately.",
